Spring Data JPA :
JPA --> Java Persistence API
--> A specification that defines how Java objects should be stored in databases.
--> Hibernate is the implementation of JPA.
JPA = Rules
Hibernate = Tool implementing rules
Application
     ↓
Spring Data JPA
     ↓
Hibernate
     ↓
Database
--> Spring Data JPA handles : Session management, Transaction handling, Query execution, Object mapping & CRUD operations

Methods JpaRepository :
1. save() --> Used to insert or update a record.
Generated SQL:
INSERT INTO student(id,name)
VALUES(101,'Teju');

2. findById() --> Fetch a record using Primary Key.
Generated SQL:
SELECT * FROM student
WHERE id=101;

3. findAll() --> Retrieve all records.
Generated SQL:
SELECT * FROM student;

4. delete() --> Delete using the object.
Generated SQL:
DELETE FROM student
WHERE id=101;

5. deleteById() --> Delete directly using Primary Key.
Generated SQL:
DELETE FROM student
WHERE id=101;

6. count() --> Returns total number of records.
Generated SQL:
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM student;

7. existsById() --> Checks whether a record exists.
Generated SQL:
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM student
WHERE id=101;
